# Environment variable template
#
# Copy to `.env.local` only if you need a value locally:
#   cp .env.example .env.local
# `.env.local` is git-ignored (see .gitignore) — never commit a real value.
# This file is tracked, so it must never contain one.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The GIBS site currently requires NO environment variables.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Verified: there are no `import.meta.env`, `process.env`, or `VITE_*` references
# anywhere in src/ or index.html, and the production build makes zero network
# requests. Fonts, images and data are all self-hosted and compiled into the
# bundle, so `npm run build` is fully self-contained.
#
# This file exists so that a future variable has an obvious, secret-free home
# rather than being invented ad hoc.
#
# Rules for anything added below:
#   - VITE_*  -> compiled into the PUBLIC browser bundle. NEVER put a secret
#                here. No value prefixed VITE_ is confidential, ever.
#   - no prefix -> server-only, used inside Vercel Functions. Safe for secrets.
#   - prefer Vercel project environment variables for anything deployed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Observed locally in .env.local; referenced by no source or config file.
# It is a Vercel CLI/deploy credential, not an application setting. Its presence
# is unreviewed — confirm whether any tooling still needs it before relying on
# it, and store it in Vercel project env vars rather than on disk.
# Value intentionally omitted.
VERCEL_OIDC_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# No backend environment variables.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# There is no database, no API, and no serverless function in the current GIBS
# architecture. The site is a static build rendered from src/lib/data.ts, and the
# contact workflow is a validated mailto: link. Nothing below this line is
# required, and no Vercel Function reads any variable.
#
# Archived backend material once used GIBS_DATABASE_URL, GIBS_DATABASE_SSL and
# GIBS_CORS_ORIGIN for a PostgreSQL catalogue API that was never deployed. Those
# variables have been removed rather than left here as an invitation to wire up
# code that has no role in this product.